    "body": "## 🚀 ReleaseFetch – Performance & Stability Update\r\n\r\n### ⚡ Performance Improvements\r\n- Optimized release list rendering for smoother scrolling and better responsiveness.\r\n- Reduced unnecessary recompositions and redundant UI processing.\r\n- Improved repository URL input responsiveness and interaction handling.\r\n- Refined loading behavior for a more consistent experience.\r\n\r\n### 📦 GitHub API Pagination\r\n- Reduced release batch size from 10 to 5 releases.\r\n- Implemented true GitHub API pagination.\r\n- Automatically loads the next 5 releases as you scroll.\r\n- Improved page caching and duplicate request prevention.\r\n- Avoids unnecessary network requests when revisiting previously loaded releases.\r\n\r\n### 🛠️ Bug Fixes & Stability\r\n- Improved release data handling and pagination reliability.\r\n- Strengthened loading state management and caching.\r\n- Verified release Kotlin compilation and R8 minification.\r\n- Executed unit and Robolectric tests for better reliability.\r\n\r\n### ✨ Additional Improvements\r\n- Focused on smoother performance, especially on low-end Android devices.\r\n- Preserved the existing Material 3 design and core app functionality.\r\n- Improved overall consistency and maintainability.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Developer:** Subham (Tombytee) 🇮🇳\r\n\r\n**Pakistan, Get Fucked! 🇵🇰🤡**"
  },
